{"node":{"id":"MONDO:0011946","label":"diaphanospondylodysostosis","definition":"Diaphanospondylodysostosis is characterized by absent ossification of the vertebral bodies and sacrum associated with variable anomalies. It has been described in less than ten patients from different families. Manifestations include a short neck, a short wide thorax, a reduced number of ribs, a narrow pelvis, and inconstant anomalies such as myelomeningocele, cystic kidneys with nephrogenic rests, and cleft palate.","synonyms":["vertebral ossification, defect in, with nephrogenic rests"],"xrefs":["GARD:0016674","MEDGEN:374993","MESH:C564305","OMIM:608022","Orphanet:66637","SCTID:721094006","UMLS:C1842691","icd11.foundation:508093071"],"parents":[],"parents_labels":{},"children":[],"children_labels":{},"in_core":false,"cluster_id":null,"is_group":false,"n_genes":1,"n_phenotypes":52,"mechanism_classes":[]},"genes":[{"id":"e_3b03cfdd8e0d","source":"MONDO:0011946","target":"BMPER","type":"caused_by","evidence":[{"db":"Orphanet","origin":"Orphanet","record":"ORPHA:66637","level":"curated","date":"2026-06-23","url":"https://www.orpha.net/en/disease/detail/66637","confidence":0.95,"snippet":"Disease-causing germline mutation(s) (loss of function) in (Assessed) — BMP binding endothelial regulator"},{"db":"HPO","origin":"Orphanet","record":"ORPHA:66637","level":"curated","date":"2026-09-02","confidence":0.9,"url":"https://hpo.jax.org/browse/disease/ORPHA:66637","snippet":"BMPER is annotated as disease gene of ORPHA:66637 (HPO genes_to_phenotype, Orphanet-derived)"}],"contradicting":[],"confidence":0.95,"independent_sources":["Orphanet"],"level":"curated"}],"phenotypes":[{"edge":{"id":"e_e66cf70e5be9","source":"MONDO:0011946","target":"HP:0008435","type":"has_phenotype","evidence":[{"db":"HPO","origin":"OMIM","record":"OMIM:608022 · PMID:30006055","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/30006055/","level":"observed","date":"2022-12-10","confidence":1.0,"snippet":"Diaphanospondylodysostosis: Absen